# 2024-08-06 21:00:07.568397
+Illumin8 is a flexible and intelligent REST API for persisting heterogeneous datasets in a SQLite database using Prisma and OpenRouter.

# 2024-08-06 21:00:38.741119
+## Submitting Data

# 2024-08-06 21:01:15.774484
+To submit data to the API, send a POST request to `/datasets` with the JSON data in the request body. The API will automatically determine the best schema for storing the data.

# 2024-08-06 21:01:32.151085
+### Examples

# 2024-08-06 21:01:38.503218
+1. Submit a simple object:

# 2024-08-06 21:02:04.242371
+```bash

# 2024-08-06 21:02:21.429591
+curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"name": "John", "age": 30}' http://localhost:3000/datasets

# 2024-08-06 21:02:39.139557
+2. Submit an array of objects:

# 2024-08-06 21:03:08.274001
+```bash

# 2024-08-06 21:03:21.291613
+curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '[{"title": "Book 1", "author": "Author 1"}, {"title": "Book 2", "author": "Author 2"}]' http://localhost:3000/datasets

# 2024-08-06 21:03:42.237576
+3. Submit nested objects:

# 2024-08-06 21:04:22.725777
+```bash

# 2024-08-06 21:04:34.769760
+curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"user": {"name": "Alice", "email": "alice@example.com"}, "order": {"items": [{"product": "Product 1", "quantity": 2}, {"product": "Product 2", "quantity": 1}], "total": 100}}' http://localhost:3000/datasets

# 2024-08-06 21:05:10.421129
+## Querying Data

# 2024-08-06 21:06:15.356191
+To query the stored data, you can use the Prisma Client in your application code. Here are some examples:

# 2024-08-06 21:07:05.022131
+1. Get all datasets:

# 2024-08-06 21:07:22.146351
+```typescript

# 2024-08-06 21:07:34.620987
+const datasets = await prisma.dataset.findMany();

# 2024-08-06 21:08:03.269808
+```

# 2024-08-06 21:08:16.367277
+2. Get a specific dataset by ID:

# 2024-08-06 21:08:58.957046
+```typescript

# 2024-08-06 21:09:11.069830
+const dataset = await prisma.dataset.findUnique({ where: { id: 1 } });

# 2024-08-06 21:09:23.363734
+```

# 2024-08-06 21:09:41.222279
+3. Query datasets based on specific conditions:

# 2024-08-06 21:10:06.831064
+```typescript

# 2024-08-06 21:10:17.447553
+const datasets = await prisma.dataset.findMany({

# 2024-08-06 21:10:37.275835
+  where: {

# 2024-08-06 21:10:59.924288
+    data: {

# 2024-08-06 21:11:24.167844
+      path: ['user', 'email'],

# 2024-08-06 21:11:45.934269
+      equals: 'alice@example.com',

# 2024-08-06 21:12:09.534972
+    },

# 2024-08-06 21:12:29.248034
+  },

# 2024-08-06 21:13:43.902258
+```

# 2024-08-06 21:13:54.046954
+For more advanced queries, refer to the [Prisma documentation](https://www.prisma.io/docs/concepts/components/prisma-client/querying-data).

